## Contract

Signal handler for graceful shutdown on SIGTERM/SIGINT. Sets `keep_running = 0` to signal the main loop to exit cleanly.

## Dependencies

None

## Slots

| Slot | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `keep_running` | `volatile sig_atomic_t` | Atomic flag checked by main loop to determine shutdown |
| `sig_handler(int sig)` | function | Signal callback — sets `keep_running = 0` |
| `signal_setup(void)` | function | Registers `sig_handler` for SIGTERM and SIGINT |

## Boundaries

- **Prohibited**: `malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`, `free` — signal handlers must not allocate memory
- Signal handlers must be async-signal-safe; only use async-signal-safe functions

## Examples

```c
// Signal handler — graceful shutdown for SIGTERM/SIGINT
volatile sig_atomic_t keep_running = 1;

void sig_handler(int sig) {
    keep_running = 0;
}

void signal_setup(void) {
    signal(SIGTERM, sig_handler);
    signal(SIGINT, sig_handler);
}
```
